## Data Cleanup

### On Logout
Clear ALL of the following:
1. Auth tokens from secure storage.
2. All Hive boxes (encrypted and regular).
3. In-memory caches (provider state).
4. Image/thumbnail caches.
5. Pending API request queues.
6. Session timers and background tasks.

```dart
class DataCleanupService {
  Future<void> clearAllData() async {
    await _secureStorage.deleteAll();
    await Hive.deleteFromDisk();
    // Invalidate all Riverpod providers
    // Cancel all pending timers and streams
    // Clear image cache
    imageCache.clear();
    imageCache.clearLiveImages();
  }
}
```

### On Account Deletion
Same as logout, plus:
- Remove device registration from backend.
- Clear push notification tokens.
- Delete any downloaded recordings.

## Rules

- NEVER store tokens in SharedPreferences or regular Hive boxes.
- NEVER log sensitive data — tokens, passwords, personal information.
- NEVER disable TLS validation in production builds.
- NEVER skip biometric auth for sensitive operations.
- NEVER persist streaming URLs or RTSP credentials to disk.
- NEVER allow cleartext HTTP traffic in production.
- ALWAYS use `flutter_secure_storage` for authentication tokens.
- ALWAYS use encrypted Hive boxes for cached user/camera data.
- ALWAYS implement session timeout (15 minutes inactive).
- ALWAYS enable certificate pinning in production builds.
- ALWAYS clear all data on logout — leave no traces.
- ALWAYS require TLS 1.3 for all network connections.
- ALWAYS sanitize error messages before logging or displaying.
